⍝@ test3.

      ⎕←Q←1+⊂2 3
 3 4 

      ]OWNERS

      ⍝ regression (Bugs28 #97): ]OWNERS asserted ufun||fun->is_native()
      ⍝ for an NC_FUNCTION/NC_OPERATOR value-stack item, but the LO/RO
      ⍝ operand of a called defined operator can hold a *primitive*
      ⍝ function, for which get_func_ufun() is 0 and is_native() is
      ⍝ false -- crashing the interpreter whenever ]OWNERS ran while
      ⍝ such an operator was suspended (e.g. ÷OP1 0 below, with
      ⍝ LO←÷ still localised). Symbol::unmark_all_values() already
      ⍝ documented and correctly skipped exactly this case; show_owners()
      ⍝ now does the same instead of asserting.
      ⍝
      ⎕FX 'Z←(LO OP1) B' 'Z←LO B'
OP1

      ÷OP1 0
DOMAIN ERROR
OP1[1]  Z←LO B
          ^

      ]OWNERS

      )SIC
      )ERASE OP1

